    "id": "train-5453",
    "question": "It takes Bryan 5 minutes to walk from his house to the bus station. Then he rides the bus for 20 minutes. After that, he walks 5 minutes from the bus station to his job. It takes the same amount of time in the morning and the evening. How many hours per year does Bryan spend traveling to and from work, if he works every day?",
    "gold": "365",
    "answer": "Bryan spends 5+20+5 =<<5+20+5=30>>30 minutes traveling to work.\nHe does this twice a day, so he spends 30*2=<<30*2=60>>60 minutes traveling per day.\nThus, he spends 60/60=<<60/60=1>>1 hour traveling to and from work every day.\nThus, he spends 1 hour*365 days =<<1*365=365>>365 hours traveling per year.\n#### 365"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many hours per year Bryan spends traveling to and from work, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total time Bryan spends traveling to work in one day.\n2. Calculate the total time Bryan spends traveling to work in one year.\n3. Convert the total travel time from minutes to hours.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total time Bryan spends traveling to work in one day.**\n\nBryan's travel time to work consists of:\n- Walking from his house to the bus station: 5 minutes\n- Riding the bus: 20 minutes\n- Walking from the bus station to his job: 5 minutes\n\nAdding these times together, we get:\n\\[ 5 + 20 + 5 = 30 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nSince the same amount of time is spent traveling to work in the morning and the evening, the total time spent traveling to work in one day is:\n\\[ 30 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the total time Bryan spends traveling to work in one year.**\n\nBryan works every day of the year, so the total time spent traveling to work in one year is:\n\\[ 30 \\text{ minutes/day} \\times 365 \\text{ days/year} = 10950 \\text{ minutes/year} \\]\n\n**Step 3: Convert the total travel time from minutes to hours.**\n\nThere are 60 minutes in an hour, so we convert 10950 minutes to hours by dividing by 60:\n\\[ \\frac{10950}{60} = 182.5 \\text{ hours/year} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total time Bryan spends traveling to and from work per year is:\n\\[ \\boxed{182.5} \\]",
